From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Kane <jameskane@ieee.org>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 22:00:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] [VectraOS] clang Driver: add the VectraOS toolchain for
 croi's programs

Adds clang/lib/Driver/ToolChains/VectraOS.{h,cpp}: a Generic_ELF-derived
toolchain for the *-vectraos triple, with its own linker tool, adapted
from swift-on-vectra's toolchain for *-vectraos.

VectraOS's tier 1 programs reach croi through libsys, with no POSIX
library beneath them, and are linked as VectraOS links its tier 0
programs (cmake/croi.cmake). So, by default:

  - static, non-PIE ET_EXEC at --image-base=0x1000000, entered at
    _start, -z separate-loadable-segments, -z stack-size=262144; -pie is
    refused; -shared links nothing by default (a library dlopen loads
    takes libc, libsys and Sys from its program)
  - tier 1's start file, crt1.o, first when the sysroot has one
  - --build-id=sha1, -z max-page-size=0x1000, -z noexecstack, -z now
  - default libraries: -lc++ -lc++abi for C++, then libsys and
    VectraOS's libc and libm, grouped since they call each other
    (-lsys -lc -lm), then -lclang_rt.builtins
  - one sysroot: <sysroot>/usr/include, <sysroot>/usr/include/c++/v1,
    <sysroot>/usr/lib; no GCC discovery, multilib or multiarch
  - DWARF 5 by default
  - frame pointers in every function, leaf functions included on
    AArch64, since VectraOS's tracer and debugger walk them
  - compiler-rt, libc++, asynchronous unwind tables; C++ exceptions off
    until the C++ runtime has an unwinder (M6d)
